Restoration/cache procedure for each later authorized runtime mutation:
- Start each mutation in a fresh shell. Before mutation record the source SHA-256
  above and `stat -f %m` (baseline source mtime 1792106981 at this freeze).
- Make a unique `backup=$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/aq0-source.XXXXXX")`, copy the
  resolver byte-for-byte to it, install an EXIT/HUP/INT/TERM trap that copies the
  backup back, touches the resolver to force Cargo cache invalidation, verifies
  its SHA-256 equals the frozen baseline, runs `git diff --exit-code --` for the
  resolver and integration test, and deletes only that unique backup.
- Apply exactly one named patch; touch the resolver before its focused command
  so the mutation is compiled. Never overlap a mutation or reuse a mutant build
  as baseline evidence. Keep test fixtures and every other guard unchanged.
- On trap restoration, the fresh mtime is deliberately newer than mutant build
  artifacts. Record restored SHA, mtime, and clean diff before the next mutant;
  the final focused positive command must compile the restored source again.

